{"text": "Cold Mornings.\n\nOmar is new in this city. It is a very cold city. There is snow on every street.\n\nOmar is thirty-four. He is from Morocco. He knows no one here.\n\nBut every morning at seven, someone waves.\n\nIt is a little girl. She lives in the window across the street. She has a yellow hat. She has a big smile.\n\nOmar waves, too. The girl smiles.\n\nBut her eyes are not on his face. She always looks down a little.\n\nWhat does she see?\n\nOmar makes bread. He works in a small bread shop. The shop is under his flat.\n\nEvery day, he makes many kinds of bread. He also makes his mother's bread. It is thin and flat. It is the bread of his home.\n\nPeople come in from the snow. They buy bread. They say, \"Thank you.\" Omar says, \"Thank you,\" too.\n\nThat is all. Omar is shy. He does not know many words here.\n\nIn the evening, the street is quiet.\n\nOmar eats his dinner alone. He drinks hot green tea. He reads his mother's letters.\n\nHis flat is small. It has no fridge.\n\nSo Omar puts a cup of milk outside. It stands on the window. It is cold there.\n\nEvery evening, the cup is full.\n\nBut every morning, the cup is not full.\n\nOmar looks at the cup. He looks at the snow on the window. There are small holes in it. They look like little flowers.\n\n\"Is it the wind?\" he asks. \"Is it a bird?\"\n\nHe does not know. At seven, he goes to the window.\n\nThe girl is there. She smiles at his window. Omar smiles, too. This is the best time of his day.\n\nOmar wants to say hello. He wants to say more.\n\nAt night, he practises his words. \"Good morning. My name is Omar. Do you like bread?\"\n\nBut Omar is very, very shy.\n\nOne night, there is a lot of snow. The wind is strong. Only the bread shop is warm. It is warm all night.\n\nIn the morning, Omar goes to his window. The cup is full. There are no holes in the snow.\n\nThe girl is at her window. But she does not wave. She does not smile.\n\nShe cries.", "textSha256": "673149a21ca7f350e9facfb80f8ea7475